; A value expression must consume its whole input: text left over after a
; complete expression is a parse error, not silently dropped.

2024/01/05 Grocer
    Expenses:Food                 $15.00
    Assets:Cash

test eval '1 2' -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing value expression:
  1 2
    ^
Error: Unexpected value '2'
end test

test eval ') 1' -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing value expression:
  ) 1

Error: Unexpected expression token ')'
end test

test reg --limit ') junk' -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing value expression:
  ) junk

Error: Unexpected expression token ')'
end test

test reg --display 'and' -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing value expression:
  and

Error: Unexpected expression token '&'
end test
